OL,1,Vk4                               G3/8
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGHURD DISMAYED OVER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLITHUANIA MOVE
OL,4,D
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Douglas Hurd has said
OL,6, he is dismayed by President Gorbachev's
OL,7, threat to apply economic sanctions
OL,8, against Lithuania.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe announcement that the republic was
OL,11,Fbeing given until Sunday to rescind
OL,12,Flaws passed since its declaration of
OL,13,Findependence came only two days after
OL,14,Fthe Soviet leader met Mr Hurd.
OL,16,FHe said he had been assured then that
OL,17,Fthere would be no sanctions.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMr Hurd warned that there would be a
OL,20,Fpenalty to pay in the USSR's relations
OL,21,Fwith the West if coercion was used.
OL,23,D]FFromG14-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
