OL,1,Vk4                               G4/8
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA CRITICISES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSANCTIONS EASING
OL,4,D
OL,5, Mrs Thatcher's easing of sanctions
OL,6, against South Africa is "absolutely
OL,7, disastrous" Nelson Mandela has said.
OL,9,FSpeaking before his visit to Britain,
OL,10,Fthe African National Congress deputy
OL,11,Fleader ruled out any meeting with the
OL,12,FPrime Minister this week.
OL,14,FMr Mandela said he was keen to improve
OL,15,Frelations with the British government,
OL,16,Fbut "it was regrettable that Mrs
OL,17,FThatcher has taken a unilateral action"
OL,18,                     F
OL,19,FHowever, he was highly critical of the
OL,20,FPrime Minister's planned meeting next
OL,21,Fmonth with President de Klerk.
OL,23,D]FFromG14-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
